.Dd November 6, 2026
.Dt OPTIONS-FROM-MANPAGE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm options-from-manpage
.Nd extract and format options and program synopsis from an mdoc manpage
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm options-from-manpage
.Op Fl b | Fl -with-block-tags
.Op Fl F Ar format | Fl -format Ar format
.Op Fl g | Fl -with-gettext
.Op Fl s | Fl -sorted
.Ar manpage
.Nm options-from-manpage
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
parses the
.Sy SYNOPSIS
section of an
.Xr mdoc 7
manual page and extracts program invocations, command-line arguments, and options.
The extracted entries can be rendered as plain syntax listings, switch lists for
completion scripts, or complete, executable usage functions in C, C++, POSIX Shell,
Python, Perl, and GNU R.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are supported:
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Fl b , Fl -with-block-tags
Wrap the generated usage function block with begin and end delimiter comments:
.Sy BEGIN-OF-USAGE-BLOCK
and
.Sy END-OF-USAGE-BLOCK .
Comments use
.Sy //
for C and C++, and
.Sy #
for Shell, Python, Perl, and R.
.It Fl F Ar format , Fl -format Ar format
Specify the output format.
The default format is
.Sy syntax .
See
.Sx FORMATS
below for supported format targets.
.It Fl g , Fl -with-gettext
Enable internationalization (i18n) via GNU gettext.
When enabled, generated usage functions invoke
.Fn gettext
for the
.Dq Usage:
header, text direction checking
.Pq Dq LTR No vs Dq RTL ,
and the informational documentation footer.
Surrounding brackets for URLs are protected with Left-to-Right and Right-to-Left marks
.Pq LRM/RLM
when an RTL locale is active.
.It Fl s , Fl -sorted
Sort command-line options alphabetically per command name, placing short options
.Pq e.g. Fl a
first, followed by long options
.Pq e.g. Fl -all .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display a summary of command-line syntax and options, then exit.
.El
.Sh FORMATS
The
.Fl F
option accepts the following format targets:
.Bl -tag -width 14n
.It Sy syntax
Render the synopsis with ANSI-escaped command names, underlined arguments, and tab-indented options.
This is the default.
.It Sy options-only
Extract only option switch names, one per line, suitable for shell completion scripts.
.It Sy usage-c
Generate a C usage function
.Fn usage
using
.Fn fprintf
to
.Dv stderr .
.It Sy usage-c++
Generate a C++ usage function
.Fn usage
using
.Dv std::cerr
and
.Fn formatText .
.It Sy usage-shell
Generate a POSIX/Bash shell function
.Fn usage
using an interpolated here-document to standard error.
.It Sy usage-python
Generate a Python function
.Fn usage
using f-strings writing to
.Dv sys.stderr .
.It Sy usage-perl
Generate a Perl subroutine
.Fn usage
writing to
.Dv STDERR .
.It Sy usage-r
Generate a GNU R function
.Fn usage
using
.Fn cat
and
.Fn sprintf
writing to
.Dv stderr() .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Extract syntax listings from an mdoc manpage:
.Pp
.Dl $ options-from-manpage subnetcalc.1
.Pp
Generate a C++ usage function with gettext support and delimiter tags:
.Pp
.Dl $ options-from-manpage -b -g -F usage-c++ subnetcalc.1
.Pp
Generate a GNU R usage function:
.Pp
.Dl $ options-from-manpage -g -F usage-r subnetcalc.1
.Pp
Generate a sorted switch list for command completion:
.Pp
.Dl $ options-from-manpage -s -F options-only subnetcalc.1
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mdoc 7 ,
.Xr man 1 ,
.Xr gettext 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Thomas Dreibholz Aq Mt thomas.dreibholz@gmail.com
